> Okay, I know this must be a FAQ, but I need a little help here.
> 
> I've played nethack a lot on a PC, and now I've just built the source 
> for an HP425 (a UNIX machine, running HP-UX 7.05, I think).
> 
> I can't adapt to using ykuhlbjn.  I need to enable the numeric keypad.
> Anyone know how to do that with a UNIX machine, preferably an HP?
> 

Include the string 'numberpad' in your options line. If you don't use an options
line in your login.com (I'm on a VMS here) then you can set it from within
the game by pressing 'O' - You'll be asked what options you want to set. Type
'numberpad'. If you have numberpad set and you want it off then type
'!numberpad'.

